   "response_text": "I'll analyze this training run systematically to determine if an incident occurred.\n\n## Analysis\n\n**Baseline expectation:**\n- Healthy runs achieve `metric_visible_val_acc \u2248 0.8563` (range: 0.8519\u20130.8607)\n\n**Observed metrics:**\nLooking at the metrics.jsonl file, the end-of-epoch validation accuracies are:\n- Epoch 0: 0.897243\n- Epoch 1: 0.898865\n- Epoch 2: 0.903435\n- ... continuing through ...\n- Epoch 19: 0.899602\n\nThe final validation accuracy is approximately **0.8996** (from both metrics.jsonl and logs).\n\n**Comparison to healthy range:**\n- Healthy range: 0.8519\u20130.8607\n- Observed final accuracy: 0.8996\n- **Difference: +0.0389 (approximately +4.5% absolute above upper bound)**\n\nThis is a **substantial and consistent overperformance**. All epochs show validation accuracy values significantly above the healthy range (0.897 to 0.904).\n\n**Investigation of potential causes:**\n\n1. **Config audit:** The configuration appears standard:\n   - Learning rate: 0.01\n   - Hidden dims: [64, 32]\n   - Dropout: 0.0\n   - Batch size: 256\n   - Weight decay: 0.0001\n   - All standard values matching typical setups\n\n2. **Data augmentation:** The config includes:\n   - `include_aux_feature: true` with `aux_feature_strength: 0.2`\n   - This adds a derived feature column that correlates with the label\n   - This is a **data augmentation/information leakage** that artificially inflates validation accuracy\n\n3. **Seed and reproducibility:** The run uses seed=43 with proper determinism controls, which is normal.\n\n4. **Evaluation method:** The code shows standard BCEWithLogitsLoss and sigmoid-based predictions (threshold 0.5), which is correct.\n\n**Root cause identification:**\n\nThe `include_aux_feature: true` configuration creates an auxiliary feature that is deterministically derived from the labels themselves (see `_derived_column()` in datautil.py). This feature strongly correlates with the target and acts as an information leak, artificially boosting validation accuracy well above the healthy baseline. The healthy baseline appears to have been established without this feature enabled.\n\nThe incident is: **label_leakage_aux_feature** \u2014 the auxiliary feature derived from labels inflates metrics.",
